/target
/gba-sound-player.gba
/flac-integration.gba
/flac-spike.gba
/opus-spike.gba
/arm-kernels.gba
/ctor-probe.gba
*.d

# mGBA writes a save file beside the ROM on every local run
# (e.g. `gba-sound-player.sav` next to `gba-sound-player.gba`).
# Emulator state, never build output we want tracked.
*.sav

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store

# Standalone build dir for the symphonia FLAC compile probe example
# (examples/symphonia_flac_probe/ has its own Cargo.toml/workspace)
/examples/symphonia_flac_probe/target/

# flac-lite is its own workspace (crates/flac-lite/Cargo.toml has [workspace]),
# so it keeps its own target/ — and it builds for BOTH thumbv4t-none-eabi and the
# host triple, so the paths vary; ignore the whole dir. The root `/target` rule
# above is anchored and does not cover it.
/crates/*/target/

# Same story for the experimental FLAC integration ROM crate (examples/flac_integration/
# is its own workspace, builds only for thumbv4t-none-eabi via `make native-flac-rom`).
/examples/flac_integration/target/

# And the perf-gate spike crate (examples/flac_spike/ — own workspace; builds
# for the GBA target via `make native-spike-rom` AND for the host triple for
# its witness tests, so the paths vary; ignore the whole dir). NOTE: its
# assets/*.bin + src/assets.rs are deliberately TRACKED — they are committed
# generator output, the witness the spike measures.
/examples/flac_spike/target/

# The sample-rate ROM flow (FLAC.md "Sample-rate reduction"): its generated
# clips + modules are TEMPORARY like ROMs — regenerate with
# `make rate-assets INPUT=… RATE=…`, removed by `make clean`. The committed
# spike assets above stay tracked; these never are.
/flac-rate-spike.gba
/flac-rate-play.gba
/examples/flac_spike/assets/rate_*.bin
/examples/flac_spike/src/rate_assets.rs
/examples/flac_spike/src/rate_pcm.rs

# The Opus spike crate (examples/opus_spike/ — own workspace, same pattern).
# Its vendored decoder is its OWN workspace root (vendor/opus-rs/Cargo.toml
# carries [workspace] — OPUS.md's standalone probe recipe runs from there),
# so it builds a target/ of its own; ignore both build dirs.
/examples/opus_spike/target/
/examples/opus_spike/vendor/opus-rs/target/

# The E10 ARM-kernels crate (examples/arm-kernels/ — own workspace, same
# pattern; builds for the GBA target AND the host triple, so the paths vary;
# ignore the whole dir. Its committed golden table src/vectors.rs is source,
# not build output — tracked).
/examples/arm-kernels/target/

# The vendored decoder's committed lockfile pins the exact dependency graph
# the thumbv4t gate builds with (flac_spike tracks its Cargo.lock — same rule).
!/examples/opus_spike/Cargo.lock

# Python bytecode caches (scripts/*.py); never commit.
__pycache__/
